"freETarget" is the name of that project; FeT Monitor does not use it as its own.

fetserver/esptool_shim/ is not under the MIT License: it holds three stub flasher files from esptool 4.7.0
(Espressif Systems, https://github.com/espressif/esptool, tag v4.7.0; the stubs' source is its flasher_stub/
folder) and a small launcher, all under esptool's license, GPL-2.0-or-later (fetserver/esptool_shim/LICENSE).
Debian's esptool package leaves those stubs out; the flash station runs esptool through the launcher as a separate
program so it can write the ESP32-S3 board.

